From b2f4a4ff238244707ea3b4fe78e59c16e2143e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:36:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add structured match events with one match id and stage
 timing.

Card server and matchmaker write one JSON line per match step to
Logs/events (card insert, queue, room, match found, peer connect,
loading, battle, result, disconnect, room end). A background writer
masks and writes them, rotates daily, keeps 14 days and caps the folder
at 200 MB. A full queue drops events instead of slowing requests.

The matchmaker names each room m-<boot>-<room>. The card server gets the
boot id from the optional boot field in GET /status and rebuilds the id
from the room the cabinet reports, so no game reply changes.

Stages slower than configurable limits log gap_warning, and
tools/match-timeline rebuilds one match from events files. Card ids,
access codes, serials, secrets and IPs never appear; tests enforce it.
Text logs are unchanged and StructuredLog.Enabled=false turns it off.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
